eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-13 : List Word
eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-13 = unlines (cons "In “Eye Contact: Co-Processing at the Speed of Light” (Part 7 of the Information Dynamic series), on the evolution of eye contact, the coupling through light of two people's nervous systems:" (cons "Evolution of Eye Contact" (cons "Humans evolved specialized machinery for this coupling:" (cons "Visible sclera (whites of eyes):" (cons "Unique among primates" (cons "Makes gaze direction obvious from distance" (cons "Allows others to see what you're attending to" (cons "Creates vulnerability (your attention is observable) AND coordination capacity (shared attention, joint action)" (cons "Complex periocular musculature:" (cons "Enables subtle expressions around eyes" (cons "Orbicularis oculi (crow's feet), corrugator supercilii (furrowed brow), etc." (cons "High-resolution emotional signaling" (cons "Specialized neural processing:" (cons "Fusiform face area (ventral visual stream): dedicated to face recognition" (cons "Superior temporal sulcus: processes eye gaze and biological motion" (cons "Amygdala: responds to direct gaze (threat/approach detection)" (cons "We're adapted for sophisticated visual coupling. Selection pressure makes sense:" (cons "Cooperation requires coordination (joint attention, shared goals)" (cons "Competition requires threat assessment (who's watching, dominance signaling)" (cons "Mate selection requires interest detection (mutual attraction, compatibility)" (cons "Social learning requires attention tracking (see what teacher is looking at)" (cons "Organisms that could read and signal internal states through eye contact cooperated and competed more effectively. The coupling machinery was selected because it enabled better information exchange about internal processing." nil))))))))))))))))))))))
